    "https://www.jobs.gla.ac.uk/job/receptionist-6069582": {
      "title": "Receptionist · University of Glasgow",
      "description": "Receptionist · University of Glasgow This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience. read more Got it! Vacancies About Us Contact Why UofG Login Register Login Menu Vacancies About Us Why UofG Contact Sign In Home Jobs Receptionist Receptionist Back to jobs Receptionist Job details Posted 26 October 2026 Salary £25,804 pa - £27,319 pa Location Glasgow Job Type Management Professional & Administrative Reference 211293 Expiry 09 Nov 2026 23:45 Job description Please note this vacancy is open to current University of Glasgow employees only. Job Purpose To provide excellent and professional customer service as the first point of contact at the Adam Smith Business School reception and deliver comprehensive administrative support across a range of operational activities. Main Duties and Responsibilities 1. Reception Services: - Deliver high-quality customer service to staff, students, and visitors in person, by phone, and online. - Maintain a professional and welcoming reception environment. 2. Operational Support: - Assist with booking meeting rooms and managing space access systems (e.g., security cards). - Maintain stationery and supplies to meet operational demand. - Support purchasing and procurement processes. 3. Facilities Coordination: - Log and follow up on maintenance requests. - Coordinate with Estates and IT teams to ensure equipment and facilities are functioning and well-maintained. 4. Student and Academic Support: - Respond to student enquiries at reception and direct them to appropriate teams. - Provide support for learning and teaching activities as required. 5. Administrative Assistance: - Offer general administrative support to School colleagues. - Assist with documentation, scheduling, and internal communications. - Any other required tasks consummate with the grade Knowledge, Qualifications, Skills & Experience Knowledge & Qualifications Essential: A1 SCQF Level 5 or 6 (e.g., National 5 or 6, SVQ Level 2 or 3), or equivalent experience in a similar role. Desirable: B1 Familiarity with University systems such as MyCampus, Salto Space, and Moodle. Skills Essential: C1 Excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. C2 Strong organisational and prioritisation abilities. C3 Ability to work independently and as part of a team. C4 Discretion, tact, and professionalism. Experience Essential: E1 Previous experience in a receptionist or administrative role. E2 Demonstrated ability to manage varied tasks in a busy environment. Terms and Conditions Salary will be Grade 4, £25,804 - £27,319 per annum. This post is full time and open ended. Closing date: 23:45 9th November 2026 This role is not eligible for sponsorship under the UK Skilled Worker visa route. Candidates must therefore have an existing right to work in the UK or be able to secure this independently prior to commencing employment. For further information on alternative immigration options, please visit University of Glasgow’s UKVI Website. As a valued member of our team, you can expect: 1 A warm welcoming and engaging organisational culture, where your talents are developed and nurtured, and success is celebrated and shared. 2 An excellent employment package with generous terms and conditions including 41 days of leave for full time staff, pension - pensions handbook https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/payandpensions/pensions/, benefits and discount packages. 3 A flexible approach to working. 4 A commitment to support your health and wellbeing, including a free 6-month UofG Sport membership for all new staff joining the University  https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/staff/healthwellbeing/. We believe that we can only reach our full potential through the talents of all. Equality, diversity and inclusion are at the heart of our values. Applications are particularly welcome from across our communities and in particular people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented within the University. Read more on how the University promotes and embeds all aspects of equality and diversity within our community https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/. We endorse the principles of Athena Swan https://www.gla.ac.uk/myglasgow/humanresources/equalitydiversity/athenaswan/ and hold bronze, silver and gold awards across the University. We are investing in our organisation, and we will invest in you too. Please visit our website https://www.gla.ac.uk/explore/jobs/ for more information. Apply Now Save this job Receptionist Glasgow Posted about 16 hours ago Apply Now Share this job linkedin twitter facebook mail whatsapp Sign up for job alerts Sign in or register here to receive emails about new jobs like these You agree to our Terms & conditions Latest Jobs Receptionist Glasgow £25,804 pa - £27,319 pa Programme and Development Manager Glasgow Grade 9, £59,966 - £67,468 per annum Graduate Teaching Assistant - School of Law Glasgow Deputy Director of Procurement Glasgow Grade 9, £59,966 - £67,468 per annum Clinical Lecturer in Child Health Glasgow Clinical Academic Scale: £52,229 - £77,389 per annum logo The University of Glasgow is a registered Scottishcharity: Registration Number SC004401 X Facebook instagram Legal Cookies Terms of use PeopleXD accessibilty statement Candidate privacy notice Accreditation Quick Links About Contact Us Vacancies Salaries Applicant Guide All Right Reserved 2026 University of Glasgow Recruitment website by"
